From cc59699af099938386c41936fee15d9e7995fb96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:59:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] PCI: apple: Adopt T6050 port 0's multi-function N1 and
 reset its root port

The N1 Wi-Fi/Bluetooth sits on apcie0 port 0, which the bootloader now
trains like ports 2 and 3. Two things the adoption assumed do not hold
for it:

- It is multi-function. In its ROM personality only function 0 answers;
  after its firmware starts, Control, Alpha and Beta (0-2) do. Each
  function's RID is routed to its own DART stream from the iommu-map
  (slot == SID) when it is enabled, instead of the one route set at
  adoption; config accesses on the adopted bus reach every function of
  device 0; teardown clears every slot it routed. Port 0 is accepted.
- Its ROM links at Gen1. Adoption takes an x1 link at Gen1 to Gen3 (the
  bootloader's target), not only Gen3; the endpoint picks the speed.
- After the ROM boot it must come back on a retrained link. The host
  provides reset_root_port for an adopted port that names its PERST# pad
  (perst<n>): PME_Turn_Off to L2, PERST#, then the T6050 port disable,
  reset, enable, configure and train sequences, with the routes and the
  MSI map rewritten in between. Tunables the boot loader copied onto the
  root port node are applied; absent ones are skipped.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 94e4ebf62104fbee3f366d0938a1311c82c1817a)
